"""Desk lighthouse, step 1 of the builder's rule: the final build first, the science after.

Writes, from the data at the top of this file (edit the script, not the outputs):
  docs/pages/desk-lighthouse-build.html              the page: form sheet, wiring sheet, templates, decisions, pins, nets, budget, parts
  docs/pages/print/desk-lighthouse-build.pdf          Letter, black only: form sheet, wiring sheet, templates (landscape), then the notes (portrait)
  docs/pages/print/desk-lighthouse-form-sheet.pdf     each sheet alone
  docs/pages/print/desk-lighthouse-wiring-sheet.pdf
  docs/pages/print/desk-lighthouse-templates.pdf      actual size: the cube's faces, the lid, the deck, the drum's flat pattern
  docs/FINAL_BUILD.md                                 the same decisions, pins, nets, budget and parts as Markdown

Reference: Huy Vector, "Lighthouse Desk Lamp", huyvector.org/decor-lamps/lighthouse-desk-lamp, read 2026-11-07. The page is a
parts list and nothing else: 0.2 mm brass sheet, 4 mm brass tube, 1 mm copper wire, a 3 V 30 rpm DC gear motor, a 39 mm Edison
LED filament, a 6 x 30 mm glass fuse, a Type-C 4.2 V charging module, a battery, an 8 cm bamboo coaster. Ours keeps the idea
(a small lighthouse on a coaster, a gear motor turning something in the lantern, an LED filament as the lamp, brass) and is its
own build otherwise: an ivory tower on a brass cube on the family's brass coaster, a fixed warm-white filament with a brass
shutter turning round it the way a real optic turns round its lamp, a reed switch so the shutter parks facing you, a white text
plaque flush in the brass at the foot, and USB power. Brass at the builder's word (2026-11-07), though the family's rule since
the drone is stainless.

The hop-drawing Router is imported from pocket_ai_assistant/edu/pages/gen/wiring_sheet.py, as the hologram's, the satellite's
and the rover's generators do; the subclass adds the pin registry and the clearance check. Every number is a listing or
datasheet figure read 2026-11-07 or an owned-part record; the check ring's thickness and the vase cap's height are the usual
sizes for those lamp parts and are flagged to be measured. Nothing here has been built."""
