         f"The lamp: a ceramic strip of LEDs, the kind inside an Edison bulb, 360° of light, hung on its own stiff leads from the nut under the roof. 2700 K, not the family's 2200 K spare (that one is amber; a lighthouse lamp is warm white, and the rule is white or warm white light). {E['i_lamp_max']:.0f} mA flat out through {E['r_lamp']:.1f} Ω, {E['lamp_w'] * 1000:.0f} mW, cool enough for a closed acrylic lantern. The hole in the ceramic marks +. If 26 mm is out of stock, the [38 mm 2700 K pack]({L['filament38']}) fits with the glass cut 12 mm taller; nine spare either way."),
